    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project significant offensive upside today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Bryce Elder, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of high-leverage order positioning and a favorable park factor, making him our anchor. **Drake Baldwin** (72.67) and **Heliot Ramos** (68.00) also emerge as core plays; **Drake Baldwin** projects for massive value if he leads off against Brandon Young, while **Heliot Ramos** is boosted by a favorable 4.89 xERA matchup and wind conditions at his home park that elevate his power ceiling. **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) and **Dominic Smith** (62.31) round out the high-floor options, both capitalizing on favorable SP skill matchups that inflate their daily efficiency beyond base projections.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jackson Merrill** (59.99) in the starting outfield over **Curtis Mead** (57.04). While **Curtis Mead** carries a respectable projection against the vulnerable pitching of Bratt, **Jackson Merrill** was prioritized due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Eu. P\u00e9rez and his high-probability stolen base potential. The optimizer weighed the scarcity of speed in our 5x5 format heavily, effectively tie-breaking the decision in favor of **Jackson Merrill**. Managers should remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Coby Mayo**. While we have modeled these lineups based on historical trends, any deviation in the actual batting order could shift the efficiency scores significantly.",
